Z||000000||Cheever2||03-11-2001||09:19 PM||||Okay, so I get 5mb of personal web page space with my cable ISP, and been waiting until I had some digital pics to use it.  So today I opened my wife's MS Picture It 2001 Platinum Edition to create a slide show page.  It went pretty well, and the preview looked fine.  But when I loaded it, somehow the Back, Home & Next buttons don't show up.  Also the background I picked is not there, it's just white.  So I went to look up what went wrong, and couldn't find it.  Guess I never saved it before the upload.<P>I'm making something new (still with the Picture It software) but from blank instead of from a prepared template kind of thing.<P>If you want to see my first attempt, it's at <A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fierofanatix/page1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.houston.rr.com/fierofanatix/page1.htm</A>  <P>My RoadRunner account will let me use FrontPage but I know nothing about it.  What can you tell me about how easy it is?<P><BR>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 03-11-2001).]||||reg||2
Z||000001||Robert||03-12-2001||07:59 PM||||Looks like you are using Microsoft Picture It now for programming.  FrontPage is a snap to work with, you can check out what I have been able to do with it for my tennis club at <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net." TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net.</A> <BR>All of your link images don’t come up on my screen, but the links work just the same.<P>Good start on your page, keep at it.<P>Robert<BR><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> <P> “If you don’t look for that parking space near the entrance, you’ll never get it”||||reg||1
